{"name":"Bluebell Frost","hex":"#9999cc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bluebell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Various flowering plants with blue, usually pendulous, flowers.\n\nIn genus Hyacinthoides\ncommon bluebell (Hyacinthoides non-scripta)\nSpanish bluebell (Hyacinthoides hispanica)\nItalian bluebell (Hyacinthoides italica)\nIn other genera\ngrape hyacinth (Muscari)\n Virginia bluebell (Mertensia virginica)\nScottish bluebell (harebell) (Campanula rotundifolia)\n\nAustralian royal bluebell (Wahlenbergia gloriosa)\nTexas bluebell (Eustoma russellianum)\ndesert bluebells or California bluebell (Phacelia campanularia)","In genus Hyacinthoides\ncommon bluebell (Hyacinthoides non-scripta)\nSpanish bluebell (Hyacinthoides hispanica)\nItalian bluebell (Hyacinthoides italica)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bluebell"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://